⚠️ **IMPORTANT: credential ladder precedence contradicts its documented ladder — `refreshTokenEnv` can be silently ignored**

The documented ladder (this file's own header, lines 178–182, and the PR description: `apiKeyEnv` → **`refreshTokenEnv`** → default Keychain slot) is not what the code does. The mint branch runs only when `stack.isEmpty`, and `stack` already includes the **default slot** (`keyEnv = entry.apiKeyEnv ?? CHATGPT_OAUTH_CREDENTIALS`):

```dart
final keyEnv =
    entry.apiKeyEnv ??
    (entry.providerType == 'chatgpt-codex'
        ? chatGptOAuthCredentialsEnvName
        : null);
...
final stack = collectKeyStack(secrets, keyEnv);
...
if (stack.isEmpty) {
  // refreshTokenEnv-only entry — mint path
  continue;
}
```

So on a machine that also holds a saved login (`CHATGPT_OAUTH_CREDENTIALS` in env or the secure store — i.e. anyone who ever ran `/provider chatgpt oauth`), a queue entry that explicitly names `refreshTokenEnv: OTHER_ACCOUNT_TOKEN` silently serves traffic with the **local stored login's account** instead of minting from the named token. Wrong-account selection with zero notice; on the headless lane it works only because no Keychain exists there.

Fix is small — consult `refreshValue` before the default slot:

```dart
if (refreshValue.isNotEmpty) { /* mint path */ }
else if (stack.isEmpty) { /* skip */ }
else { /* apiKeyEnv / default-slot path */ }
```

and pin the both-present case with a test (the current tests cover each lane separately, never the conflict). Note the README wording ("an entry with no `apiKeyEnv` resolves the saved login's Keychain slot automatically, a `refreshTokenEnv` entry mints … headless runners with no Keychain") currently matches the implementation, so either the code or the header-comment/PR ladder needs to move — but they cannot keep disagreeing about which credential wins.

