💡 **SUGGESTION: kind-shaped export name + multiple accounts silently picks the first; success output never names the entry**

`findChatGptExportEntry`: when [name] is the kind itself (`chatgpt` / `chatgpt-codex`), the first saved entry whose apiType resolves to `chatgpt-codex` wins. With several saved accounts, `fa provider export chatgpt` exports **one arbitrary (first) account** while the error path helpfully lists all saved names. And the success path prints only the `export …` lines — never which entry served them — so a multi-account user cannot tell which credential they just minted.

Cheap fixes, either suffices:

```dart
io.writeln(chatGptExportLines(accessToken: credentials.accessToken));
// one extra, non-secret line for the humans:
io.writeln('# fa: exported "${entry.name}" (${entry.baseUrl})');
```

or, on the kind-shaped path, defer to an explicit name when `entries.length > 1` and print the list instead.

